    <updated>2026-10-12T03:37:50Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/PylotLight/Surffish/releases/tag/v0.1.0"/>
    <title>Surffish 0.1.0 — Security and Session Privacy</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;Surffish 0.1.0&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An early Apple-silicon release of Surffish, a focused Electron desktop browser.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Highlights&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A resizable translucent sidebar for tabs, pinned sites, and browsing history.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A nature-photo New Tab page with compact favorite and frequent-site shortcuts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built-in downloads, network ad and tracker blocking, and optional app-level SOCKS5 proxy support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bramble password-manager integration, with vault setup in a regular browser tab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Per-site controls, Picture in Picture, and persistent site icons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Security and privacy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted app surfaces are sandboxed; navigation and privileged IPC are restricted to their expected local documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Saved session URLs remove fragments and common secret-like query parameters while preserving ordinary search parameters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bramble release metadata and downloads use the configured browser session and proxy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compatibility and limitations&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;macOS Ventura 13 or later; Apple silicon only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This build is unsigned and not notarized. macOS may require Control-click → Open or, after verifying the official app and confirming you trust it, removing its quarantine attribute with &lt;code&gt;xattr -cr /Applications/Surffish.app&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surffish starts with a fresh profile and does not import legacy Sockfish profile or vault data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content>
